that was the US Secretary of State Mike  Pompeo and the secretary of the Treasury  Stephen minuchin speaking in Washington  DC and what they've just announced as a  ratcheting up of sanctions on the  Iranian government a series of new  sanctions really have been announced  I'll just tell you some of what those  are the US Secretary of Treasury did  announce 17 new sanctions they target  Iran steel and iron industries he says  this is to further hamper the Iranian  economy and the secretary State Mike  Pompeo says that the newest sanctions on  Iran will also be targeting eight senior  officials that have allegedly plotted  attacks within the region and abroad  that's according to the Secretary of  State and just a reminder that the US  officials say these sanctions follow the  missile strikes that took place on US  bases in Iraq and that was as a result  of the killing of the Iranian general  Qasem Soleimani let's bring in our White  House correspondent Kimberly how  adjoining us from Washington you were  listening in this is really ratcheting  up as I'm saying  Kimberly of the sanctions on Iran  ratcheting it up and there was some  speculation here in Washington just  among the reporters here waiting for  this announcement to come down and the  question becomes is this also a  face-saving measure by the US president  who promised that if Iran struck back  against the United States for its  assassination of general Soleimani  that he would not hesitate to act but  then of course when those strikes came  we did see hesitation on the part of the  president at least militarily now we  have heard since then when he spoke to  the American public in the hours after  those strikes that he said in fact that  there would be sanctions but he gave no  specifics so this is something that we  have been waiting for Doreen and to put  this all into context I think it's  important to know for our viewers where  things stand with respect to sanctions  because this maximum pressure economic  campaign by the United States has been  in place for some time it started with  the withdrawal of the United States from  the agreement the jcpoa to limit Iran's  nuclear program that's when those  snapback sanctions that had been lifted  as a result of Iran signing that  agreement were put back in place then we  had more  sanctions put in place by the United  States last June hard-hitting sanctions  targeting Iran's supreme leader as well  as the foreign minister and then last  September targeting the central bank and  the sovereign wealth fund so it really  does now appear and we heard there from  the Treasury secretary they've attempted  to really not only isolate Iran from the  global financial system but really  [ __ ] it economically in terms of what  the US Secretary of State said there is  to punish it and take punitive action  for what the United States sees as its  destructive foreign policy and kimberley  interestingly the Secretary was stayed  in particular was questioned several  times by journalists on what he had been  saying the past couple of days about an  imminent threat from in Iran including  on US embassies that prompted the u.s.  to kill general Qasem Soleimani but he's  still not providing any evidence on what  that imminent threat is no you're  absolutely right that was another one of  the headlines to come out of that and  that is something that is certainly the  subject of headlines here in the United  States whether or not the President may  have tried to detract from the negative  impeachment headlines in the Senate  trial the impending Senate trial by  taking out general Soleimani in the form  of an assassination the White House is  denying that this was an assassination  for political purposes domestically but  certainly that is something that  continues to hover over this White House  in light of those briefings on Capitol  Hill  one more headline to come out of there  Darion very quickly as well is this  discussion and this once again confusing  message on US troop withdrawal we did  hear earlier from the iraqi prime  minister in a statement that in fact  there was a discussion with the  secretary of state and the iraqi prime  minister about putting in place a  delegation to in iraq a US delegation to  begin putting in place a mechanism for  the troop withdrawal but we've since  heard from the secretary of state there  and had a statement saying that isn't  the case that there's a real difference  of opinion on that and that any  delegation sent to iraq will be to  discuss  strategic partnerships not troop  withdrawal that the u.s. worked to  eradicate ISIL from the region is not  yet complete so once again confusing  messages coming out of this  administration not concrete's not only  on the innocent imminence of the threat  with regard to US interest and the need  to take out general Soleimani but also  the concern there about the troop  withdrawal Iraq saying that they need  that to begin the United States saying  not so fast  all right so Kimberly thank you for that  update from Washington let's find out if  there's been any reaction from Tehran on  these new sanctions dorset Jabari  joining us from there as we're saying  dorsa 17 new sanctions targeting steel  and iron industries in the country as  well as sanctions on eight senior  officials any reaction at all no the  iranian don't usually respond to these  kinds of sanctions this is becoming a  regular occurrence here weekly basis  there are new US sanctions announced on  various individuals we've had a plethora  of sanctions really over the past six  months on the country's supreme leader  the country's foreign minister now some  of the high-ranking officials alongside  those names including the head of the  boats force sorry at the head of the  passage forces rather that's the  volunteer branch of the Revolutionary  Guards as well as the Secretary of the  Supreme National Security Council Alisha  I'm Connie this is a body that deals  with the country's foreign policy as  well as the nuclear issues under the  guidance of the supreme leader  we also heard the name of Mawson reza  who is a former head of the  Revolutionary Guards he is now part of  the Expediency Council so these are very  high-ranking officials who will not be  affected by these sanctions they've  never set foot on the United States and  they don't have any interests in that  country these are more seen as a  symbolic move really on the part of the  US government what will likely happen is  that his explanation the Secretary of  State mark Pompeo is explanation our  reasoning behind the imminent so-called  threats from Jason  fossum Soleimani is yet to be really  flushed out there is really no actual  explanation that they have given the one  point to make here is that they believe  by taking out this general they've taken  out somebody who had very much influence  in this region he's very much more of an  ideology now in Iran the person  soleimani name is now associated with an  idea more than anything else and that's  something that they cannot really get  rid of the other point to make is that  the secretary of the Treasury secretary  Stephen Newton said that the previous US  administration gave a hundred billion  dollars to the Iranians when they signed  the jcpoa it's important to point out  that the Iranians got back 150 billion  dollars u.s. that was under sanctions  that was frozen assets in the United  States that was their money prior to  even the 1979 revolution so that those  funds were released when they signed the  jcpoa that is something the Obama  administration didn't simply give to the  Iranians these are important points to  highlight I think what we will see in  the coming days is an more sort of the  same kind of rhetoric from here that the  United States continues this policy of  economic terrorism on Iran after taking  out one of the highest-ranking generals  within the establishment a writer sir  Jabari thank you for that update from  Tehran

